{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear ye this, O priests; and hearken, ye house of Israel; and give ye ear, O house of the king; for judgment ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards you, because ye have been a snare on Mizpah, and a net spread upon Tabor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the revolters are profound to make slaughter, though I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a rebuker of them all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know Ephraim, and Israel is not hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, thou art guilty of lewdness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Israel is defiled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They will not frame their doings to turn to their God: for the spirit of lewdness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the midst of them, and they have not known the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the pride of Israel doth testify to his face: therefore shall Israel and Ephraim fall in their iniquity; Judah also shall fall with them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD; but they shall not find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; he hath withdrawn himself from them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have dealt treacherously against the LORD: for they have begotten strange children: now shall a month devour them with their portions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blow ye the cornet in Gibeah, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "at",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Beth-aven, after thee, O Benjamin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim shall be desolate in the day of rebuke: among the tribes of Israel have I made known that which shall surely be.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The princes of Judah were like them that remove the bound: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "therefore",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I will pour out my wrath upon them like water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " oppressed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " broken in judgment, because he willingly walked after the commandment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Ephraim as a moth, and to the house of Judah as rottenness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Ephraim saw his sickness, and Judah ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saw",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wound, then Ephraim went to the Assyrian, and sent to king Jareb: yet he could not heal you, nor cure you of your wound.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Ephraim as a lion, and as a young lion to the house of Judah: I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, will tear and go away; I will take away, and none shall rescue ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will go ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " return to my place, till they acknowledge their offense, and seek my face: in their affliction they will seek me early.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
